artifastring
------------------------------------------
Artifastring (artificial fast string) is a highly optimized physical simulation
of string quartet instruments (violins, violas, and cellos) for sound
synthesis.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  cygwin-devel-3.6.12-1
  libartifastring-devel-2.4-1bl2
  libartifastring0-2.4-1bl2
  libfftw3-devel-3.3.11-1
  libfftw3_3-3.3.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1
  python-artifastring-2.4-1bl2
  python3-3.12.12-1
  python312-3.12.12-1
  python312-numpy-2.5.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  eigen3-3.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libfftw3-devel-3.3.11-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  python3-3.12.12-1
  python3-devel-3.12.12-1
  python312-numpy-2.5.4-1
  swig-4.5.1-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/gperciva/artifastring

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/gperciva/artifastring/archive/release-2.4.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack artifastring-2.4-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./artifastring-2.4-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/artifastring-2.4-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/artifastring-2.4-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libartifastring0-2.4-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libartifastring-devel-2.4-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/python-artifastring-2.4-X.tar.xz

